# BASIC's truth convention: a comparison yields -1 for true and 0 for false.
# The BASIC guide has to get this right, so it is pinned by a running case
# rather than by prose.
#
# The printed values also pin the leading-space sign convention: -1 prints as
# "-1", 0 prints as " 0", so `PRINT A; B` reads "-1 0".

expect ^-1 0$
expect ^PASS$
absent ^FAIL$
